//< A failing `main` in a program that imports nothing prints its failure and its route
//<
//< The trace printer is `print_trace` in `std/lang`, which every hosted program holds
//< (`find_backtrace_symbol` in `ksplc/sema/type/env.kspls` finds it). Caution: **Do not add an
//< import.** It would hide whether the trace reaches a program that imports nothing. It stays a
//< file of its own, not a case in `stops.kspls`: `make test-llvm-abi` compiles it by path.
// EXPECT: [Kanso] Error: main() failed with code 3
// EXPECT: stack backtrace:
// EXPECT: inner at

fn inner(): I32!Sz
    throw Sz::3

fn main(): I32!Sz
    return inner()!
